  "description": "BIRSAA crystallizes in the rhombohedral crystal system with space group R -3. Reported CIF formula moiety: C48 H46 Ce6 N6 O50. From the CIF bond table, Ce1 (Ce) has 9 O neighbors; Ce1A (Ce) has 9 O neighbors; Ce1B (Ce) has 9 O neighbors; Ce1Q (Ce) has 9 O neighbors; Ce1P (Ce) has 9 O neighbors; Ce1O (Ce) has 9 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 12 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.772-3.855 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 104.36-109.64°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [Ce6O4(OH)4(H2O)6(NO3)6(C8H5O3)6]. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 4 OH (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 6 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 6 NO3 (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 4 OH (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)), 6 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)), 6 NO3 (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)).",
  "interpretation_limit": "Oxidation states, nuclearity, oxo/hydroxo bridging, core charge and ligand identities/counts require article/SI or manual verification; atom-site counts are asymmetric-unit counts, not molecular stoichiometry. Graph topology is limited to identity-symmetry bonds in the CIF table. Approximate shape is based only on bridge-unwrapped metal-site coordinates in the largest component; symmetry-related bonds or periodic structures require manual crystallographic review. Empirical formulas alone do not establish unique oxidation-state assignments or ligand connectivity; annotations above reproduce explicit structural notation only.",
